    "created_at": "2016-09-26T08:05:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-26T08:05:57Z",
    "body": "I'm fine with firing an error event rather than throwing for the constructor. Chrome's current implementation is somewhat busted anyway, so changing the behavior to something we all can more reliably implement is reasonable at this point.\n\nI presume we'd move the logic to \"run a worker\", and just fire an `error` event at the worker if the secure contexts bits and pieces failed?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
