    "created_at": "2016-09-26T14:44:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-26T14:44:27Z",
    "body": "Oh, and once Firefox moves to multiple content processes we would presumably need to change our SharedWorker implementation.  That said, I'm really not sure how that's supposed to work given what https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/workers.html#dom-sharedworker is doing, poking settings objects that are supposedly in another process and so forth...\n\nAnd for that matter, as far as I can tell it's racy: if two pages both use `new SharedWorker` at the same time, won't they both reach step 7 and hence both do \"Run a worker\"?\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
