    "created_at": "2016-09-26T14:51:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-27T08:15:17Z",
    "body": "Right, the poking of settings objects is somewhat magic and would have to be refactored. We've so far refrained from defining \"in parallel\" in too much detail, but at some point we might have to get into that and what kind of guarantees you still have (this has also come up for storage, where you have some races, but not `localStorage.x !== localStorage.x` races which would be really sad).\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
